PAGES=[page('146_page_2.jpg',284,[heading('Summary'),heading('Parabola'),paragraph('The eccentricity of the conic is e=c/a. The conic is ellipse if e<1, parabola if e=1, hyperbola if e>1.'),paragraph('a. The standard parabola symmetric with respect to the x-axis, vertex V(0,0), focus F(p,0), directrix x=−p:'),eq(r'y^2=4px'),paragraph('b. The standard parabola symmetric with respect to the y-axis, vertex V(0,0), focus F(0,p), directrix y=−p:'),eq(r'x^2=4py'),paragraph('a. The standard parabola symmetric with respect to y=k, vertex V(h,k), focus F(h+p,k), directrix x=h−p:'),eq(r'(y-k)^2=4p(x-h)'),paragraph('b. The standard parabola symmetric with respect to x=h, vertex V(h,k), focus F(h,k+p), directrix y=k−p:'),eq(r'(x-h)^2=4p(y-k)'),paragraph('The equation of the tangent to parabola y²=4px at P(x₁,y₁):'),eq(r'yy_1=2p(x+x_1)'),paragraph('The equation of any tangent to parabola y²=4px in slope-form:'),eq(r'y=mx+\frac p m'),paragraph('The line y=mx+c touches parabola y²=4px under condition:'),eq(r'y=mx+\frac p m,\quad y^2=4py'),paragraph('The normal to parabola y²=4px at P(x₁,y₁):'),eq(r'y-y_1=-\frac{y_1}{2p}(x-x_1)'),heading('Ellipse'),paragraph('a. The standard ellipse with center at the origin, semimajor a, semiminor b and major axis along x-axis:'),eq(r'\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1'),paragraph('b. The standard ellipse with center at the origin, semimajor a, semiminor b and major axis along y-axis:'),eq(r'\frac{x^2}{b^2}+\frac{y^2}{a^2}=1'),paragraph('a. The standard ellipse with C(h,k), semimajor a, semiminor b, major axis parallel to x-axis:'),eq(r'\frac{(x-h)^2}{a^2}+\frac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1'),paragraph('b. The standard ellipse with C(h,k), semimajor a, semiminor b, major axis parallel to x-axis:'),eq(r'\frac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}+\frac{(y-k)^2}{a^2}=1'),paragraph('Tangent to ellipse x²/a²+y²/b²=1 at P(x₁,y₁):'),eq(r'\frac{xx_1}{a^2}+\frac{yy_1}{b^2}=1,\quad\frac{x_1^2}{a^2}+\frac{y_1^2}{b^2}=1\ \mathrm{at}\ (x_1,y_1)'),paragraph('Any finite-slope tangent:'),eq(r'y=mx\pm\sqrt{a^2m^2+b^2}'),paragraph('The line y=mx+c touches the ellipse under:'),eq(r'c=\pm\sqrt{a^2m^2+b^2}'),note('A conic’s focus/directrix definition uses e=d(P,F)/d(P,directrix); e=c/a is the focal-distance/semimajor-or-transverse ratio for ellipses and hyperbolas, not a definition via finite a,c for a parabola. Nondegenerate parabola requires p≠0. Its finite-slope tangent requires m≠0; the horizontal form’s vertex tangent x=0 is additional. The tangency condition line repeats y²=4py; it should retain y²=4px. The translated ellipse paragraph (b) says parallel to x-axis although its equation has vertical major axis, parallel to y. Point-form tangent/normal statements require actual curve contacts.')]),
page('147_page_1.jpg',285,[paragraph('The normal to ellipse x²/a²+y²/b²=1 at P(x₁,y₁):'),eq(r'\frac{y-y_1}{y_1/b^2}=\frac{x-x_1}{x_1/a^2}'),heading('Hyperbola'),paragraph('a. The standard hyperbola centered at the origin with x-axis as transverse axis:'),eq(r'\frac{x^2}{a^2}-\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1'),paragraph('b. The standard hyperbola centered at the origin with y-axis as transverse axis:'),eq(r'\frac{y^2}{a^2}-\frac{x^2}{b^2}=1'),paragraph('a. For horizontal standard form, the asymptotes are:'),eq(r'y=\pm\frac b a x'),paragraph('b. For vertical standard form, the asymptotes are:'),eq(r'y=\pm\frac b a x'),paragraph('a. The hyperbola centered C(h,k), vertices V₁(h+a,k),V₂(h−a,k), foci F₁(h−c,k),F₂(h+c,k):'),eq(r'\frac{(x-h)^2}{a^2}-\frac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1'),paragraph('b. The hyperbola centered C(h,k), vertices V₁(h,k+a),V₂(h,k−a), foci F₁(h,k+c),F₂(h,k−c):'),eq(r'\frac{(y-k)^2}{a^2}-\frac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1'),paragraph('a. Horizontally translated hyperbola asymptotes:'),eq(r'y-k=\pm\frac b a(x-h)'),paragraph('b. Vertically translated hyperbola asymptotes:'),eq(r'y-k=\pm\frac a b(x-h)'),paragraph('A hyperbola whose asymptotes are at right angles to each other is called a rectangular hyperbola.'),paragraph('A function of the form y=C/x is an inverse function called the rectangular hyperbola.'),paragraph('Tangent to hyperbola x²/a²−y²/b²=1 at P(x₁,y₁):'),eq(r'\frac{xx_1}{a^2}-\frac{yy_1}{b^2}=1'),paragraph('Any tangent to hyperbola x²/a²−y²/b²=1 in slope-form:'),eq(r'y=mx\pm\sqrt{a^2m^2-b^2}'),paragraph('The line y=mx+c touches the hyperbola under condition:'),eq(r'c=\pm\sqrt{a^2m^2-b^2}'),paragraph('Normal to hyperbola x²/a²−y²/b²=1 at P(x₁,y₁):'),eq(r'-\frac{x-x_1}{x_1/a^2}=\frac{y-y_1}{y_1/b^2}'),note('The vertical origin hyperbola’s asymptote slope in paragraph (b) is reversed: it should be y=±(a/b)x, matching the correctly printed translated formula. Assume a,b>0,c²=a²+b²,e=c/a>1. Its finite-slope real tangent needs a²m²−b²>0; equality gives asymptotes, and x=±a are the additional vertical tangents of the horizontal form. The rectangular reciprocal curve requires C≠0 and x≠0; y=C/x is an inverse-proportional function, not “inverse function” in the compositional sense. For normal formulas with zero coordinates, use division-free forms: ellipse (x₁/a²)(y−y₁)−(y₁/b²)(x−x₁)=0; hyperbola (x₁/a²)(y−y₁)+(y₁/b²)(x−x₁)=0.')])]
